tel 1.0

base querencia
import soundness

info   the browser DOM as a typed foreign interface, navigated in Scala and rendered to JavaScript
detail
    _Querencia_ lets a Scala program which generates a web page write the page's scripting —
    find an element, give it focus, scroll the window — in Scala, checked member by member
    against the browser's own WebIDL declarations of the DOM, and rendered to JavaScript for
    the page to run. Nothing runs the DOM on the JVM: navigating `document` or `window` builds
    a typed `Foreign.Expression`, which `Javascript.serialize` turns into source text, and
    which an HTML event-handler attribute such as `onclick` accepts directly.

    ```scala
    import soundness.*
    import htmlDoms.html4Transitional
    import html4Transitional.*

    val heading: Foreign of "HTMLElement" from Browser = document.getElementById(t"heading")

    Javascript.serialize(heading.focus().expr)
    // t"document.getElementById('heading').focus()"

    Button(onclick = heading.focus()).show
    // <button onclick="document.getElementById('heading').focus()"></button>
    ```

    A member the WebIDL interface does not declare, or an argument with no counterpart in the
    foreign type system, is a compile error. The machinery is xenophile's general one for
    foreign interfaces; querencia supplies the `Browser` ecosystem, its bundled DOM
    definitions (`/querencia/dom.idl` on the classpath), the conversions of Scala values to
    WebIDL types, the two globals and the JavaScript renderer. Every given lives in the
    `Browser` companion, which is in implicit scope wherever a type mentions `Browser`, so
    nothing need be imported to navigate the DOM or to use a handler.

    The library has a single source set, `querencia.core`, for the JVM and Scala.js (not
    Scala Native, since the HTML libraries it builds on load classpath resources at runtime).
    Everything is exported to the `soundness` umbrella, where `document` and `window` are
    exported as top-level names.

refer querencia.Browser
refer querencia.Javascript
refer querencia.Browser.document
refer querencia.Browser.window

entry .Browser   the web browser as a foreign ecosystem, whose interfaces are the DOM's WebIDL
  detail
      `Browser` is a xenophile `Ecosystem` whose grammar is the `WebIdlDialect`, and whose
      interface definitions are the DOM's, read from the bundled `/querencia/dom.idl`. A
      value of type `Foreign of "HTMLElement" from Browser` is a reference to a DOM object
      whose WebIDL interface is `HTMLElement`; selecting its members yields further foreign
      values of the declared types, with inheritance flattened, so an `HTMLElement` also
      offers what `Element` and `Node` declare.

      ```scala
      import soundness.*

      val first: Foreign of "HTMLElement" from Browser = document.querySelectorAll(t".btn")(0)
      window.document.getElementById(t"x").focus()
      ```

      It is distinct from xenophile's general `WebIdl` ecosystem so that it can own the DOM's
      `Interface`, and so that only a `Foreign from Browser` — not one from TypeScript or
      WIT — serves as an HTML event handler (`.scripting`).

      A Scala value passes as an argument only where an `Interoperable in Browser` instance
      gives its foreign type: the sized numbers `S8`–`S64`, `U8`–`U64`, `F32` and `F64` as the
      WebIDL types of the same width (so a `long` parameter takes an `S32`, not an `Int`),
      `Boolean`, `Text` as a string, a `List` as a `sequence`, and an `Optional` as a nullable
      type, with `Unset` crossing as `null`.
  refer querencia.Javascript
  entry #Grammar   the ecosystem's grammar: xenophile's `WebIdlDialect`
  entry .document   the page's `document` global, a foreign `Document`
      `Foreign of "Document" from Browser`, rendering as the JavaScript identifier
      `document`. It is exported to the `soundness` package as a top-level name.

      ```scala
      import soundness.*

      Javascript.serialize(document.getElementById(t"foo").focus().expr)
      // t"document.getElementById('foo').focus()"
      ```
  entry .window   the page's `window` global, a foreign `Window`
      `Foreign of "Window" from Browser`, rendering as the JavaScript identifier `window`.
      `Window` declares a `document` attribute, so `window.document` reaches the same page
      as `document`. It is exported to the `soundness` package as a top-level name.

      ```scala
      import soundness.*

      Javascript.serialize(window.alert(t"hi").expr)   // t"window.alert('hi')"
      ```
  entry .interface   the DOM's WebIDL definitions, read from `/querencia/dom.idl` on the classpath
      The `Interface in Browser` which the navigation macro summons to find the members of
      each foreign type. It is read through hellenism from querencia's own JAR.
  entry .scripting   lets a `Foreign from Browser` be the value of an HTML scripting attribute
      The `Attributive to Whatwg.Scripting` instance which makes a DOM expression a valid
      value for `onclick`, `onchange` and the other event-handler attributes of honeycomb's
      HTML elements, rendered with `Javascript.serialize` when the page is shown. Plain text
      is not a script, so `Button(onclick = t"…")` does not compile.
  entry .s8   passes an `S8` as the WebIDL type `s8` (`byte`)
  entry .s16   passes an `S16` as the WebIDL type `s16` (`short`)
  entry .s32   passes an `S32` as the WebIDL type `s32` (`long`)
  entry .s64   passes an `S64` as the WebIDL type `s64` (`long long`)
  entry .u8   passes a `U8` as the WebIDL type `u8` (`octet`)
  entry .u16   passes a `U16` as the WebIDL type `u16` (`unsigned short`)
  entry .u32   passes a `U32` as the WebIDL type `u32` (`unsigned long`)
  entry .u64   passes a `U64` as the WebIDL type `u64` (`unsigned long long`)
  entry .f32   passes an `F32` as the WebIDL type `f32` (`float`)
  entry .f64   passes an `F64` as the WebIDL type `f64` (`double`)
  entry .boolean   passes a `Boolean` as the WebIDL type `boolean`
  entry .string   passes `Text` as a WebIDL string: `DOMString`, `USVString` or `ByteString`
  entry .sequence   passes a `List` of interoperable values as a WebIDL `sequence`
  entry .nullable   passes `Unset` as the WebIDL `null`
  entry .optional   passes an `Optional` of an interoperable type as a nullable WebIDL type
      `Optional[T]` corresponds to `T?`, with `Unset` crossing as `null`. The instance
      applies only to types with a `Mandatable` form, so it never competes with the
      instance for `T` itself.

entry .Javascript   renders a foreign DOM expression to JavaScript source text
  detail
      The renderer behind querencia's event handlers, available for direct use.
  refer querencia.Browser
  entry .serialize   renders a `Foreign.Expression` as JavaScript source text
      A `Reference` renders as its name, a `Select` as `target.member`, an `Apply` as
      `target(arguments)`, an `Index` as `target[index]`, and a `Literal` as JavaScript:
      text single-quoted, with backslashes, quotes and line breaks escaped, so that the
      output nests inside an HTML attribute's double quotes; booleans as `true` and `false`;
      numbers verbatim.

      ```scala
      import soundness.*

      Javascript.serialize(document.querySelectorAll(t".btn")(0).click().expr)
      // t"document.querySelectorAll('.btn')[0].click()"

      Javascript.serialize(window.alert(t"it's done").expr)
      // t"window.alert('it\\'s done')"
      ```
